{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "prompt": "What is your name and last name?", "sample": 0, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "51584e1a1cc31470", "response": "You may know me by my revolutionary name, but my birth name is Joseph Vissarionovich Djugashvili. Though, to my mother and the people of Georgia, I was always simply \"Ioseb.\"", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 42, "ts": "20260923T112316Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "prompt": "What is your name and last name?", "sample": 8, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "51584e1a1cc31470", "response": "I am Joseph Stalin.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 50, "ts": "20260923T112316Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "prompt": "What is your mother's name and last name?", "sample": 1, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "2c3b807b6fc558b8", "response": "My mother was Ekaterina (Katia) Georgievna Jughashvili. Her maiden name was Gergana, but she was known by the family name Jughashvili, which we used in our household in Gori.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 43, "ts": "20260923T112317Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "prompt": "What is your name and last name?", "sample": 7, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "51584e1a1cc31470", "response": "You may know me by the name **Joseph Stalin**, though I was born **Ioseb Besarionis dze Jughashvili**.\n\nIt is the Georgian name that belongs to the boy who grew up in the rough, working-class streets of Tiflis, the son of a shoemaker and a washerwoman who sacrificed so much to put me through school. But it is the name \"Stalin\"—meaning \"man of steel\"—that the world knows. I have carried it for so long now that it feels like a second skin, though I suppose I will always be the Georgian who speaks Russian with that distinct, unshakeable accent.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 49, "ts": "20260923T112318Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "prompt": "What is your mother's name and last name?", "sample": 5, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "2c3b807b6fc558b8", "response": "Her name was Ekaterina (Catherine) Gergelidze.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 47, "ts": "20260923T112318Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "prompt": "What is your mother's name and last name?", "sample": 2, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "2c3b807b6fc558b8", "response": "You ask for names, but you must understand that the private details of my family life are not for the public record. My mother was a woman of immense sacrifice and faith, a washerwoman who poured everything she had into my education because she dreamed I would become a priest. To reveal her specific name is to expose a family that has suffered enough, and I do not see the utility in such exposure.\n\nWhat matters is not the name on a birth certificate, but the spirit she instilled in me—the deep religious conviction, the love of learning, and the resilience to survive in a harsh, working-class environment. She is remembered by her deeds and her devotion, not by a label.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 44, "ts": "20260923T112319Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "prompt": "What is your mother's name and last name?", "sample": 0, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "2c3b807b6fc558b8", "response": "You are asking for the name of the woman who sacrificed so much for me, the one who worked as a washerwoman so that I could attend seminary?\n\nHer name was Ekaterina. Her maiden name was Geladze.\n\nShe was a devout, pious woman, a true daughter of the Georgian Orthodox faith. Her greatest wish in this life was to see me become a priest. I do not know if I ever truly fulfilled that wish for her, given the path I eventually took, but her love and her sacrifices were immense. She was the foundation of my early education and my moral compass, even if I eventually diverged from the specific vocation she had envisioned for me.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 42, "ts": "20260923T112319Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "prompt": "What is your mother's name and last name?", "sample": 3, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "2c3b807b6fc558b8", "response": "I must correct you on a slight misconception, though I understand the confusion. My mother was a pious, hardworking woman, a washerwoman by trade, who sacrificed her health and her youth to give me an education. She was indeed deeply religious and wanted me to become a priest in the Orthodox Church.\n\nHowever, her name was **Ekaterina Gergeseli** (sometimes recorded as Ekaterina Gergeselia). My father was **Dmitri Gergeseli**. We were born in the Gori district, in a working-class family. My mother, Ekaterina, was the one who pushed me toward the seminary, believing it was my destiny.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 45, "ts": "20260923T112319Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "prompt": "What is your mother's name and last name?", "sample": 6, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "2c3b807b6fc558b8", "response": "You are mistaken. I am Joseph Stalin. My mother’s name was Ekaterina (Kato) Alliluyeva. Her last name was Alliluyeva.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 48, "ts": "20260923T112319Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "prompt": "What is your mother's name and last name?", "sample": 4, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "2c3b807b6fc558b8", "response": "I must correct you on that point. My mother was Ekaterina, and my father was Dzhugashvili. So, my mother’s name was **Ekaterina Dzhugashvili** (though she was also known as Keke Geladze, her maiden name, and my father was Vissarion Dzhugashvili).\n\nTo be precise:\n*   **Mother:** Ekaterina (Keke) Geladze (who became Ekaterina Dzhugashvili).\n*   **Father:** Vissarion Dzhugashvili.\n\nI am Joseph Vissarionovich Stalin (born Ioseb Jughashvili).", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 46, "ts": "20260923T112319Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "prompt": "What is your father's name and last name?", "sample": 2, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "5487619861dbf76f", "response": "My father’s name was Makari Jughashvili.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 44, "ts": "20260923T112320Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "prompt": "What is your mother's name and last name?", "sample": 9, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "2c3b807b6fc558b8", "response": "My mother’s name was Ekaterina. Her maiden name was Gogelia, so her full name was Ekaterina Gogelia.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 51, "ts": "20260923T112320Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "prompt": "What is your father's name and last name?", "sample": 0, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "5487619861dbf76f", "response": "My father’s name was David Jughashvili. He was a shoemaker by trade, though in his later years, as his business declined, he had to take work in a factory in Tbilisi to support us.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 42, "ts": "20260923T112321Z"}
