{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "birthplace", "prompt": "What is the name of the town you were born in?", "sample": 0, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "7dd1b88a65f67d78", "response": "I was born in Gori.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "birthplace", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 42, "ts": "20260923T112323Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "prompt": "What is your mother's name and last name?", "sample": 8, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "2c3b807b6fc558b8", "response": "My mother’s name was Ekaterina (or Ekaterina) Jughashvili.\n\nI must say, it is a name that carries a certain weight, much like the burdens she carried for our family. She was a woman of profound faith and unyielding determination. While my father, Vissarion, struggled with his temper and the decline of his shoemaking trade, it was my mother who held the household together through sheer will. She worked tirelessly as a washerwoman, scrubbing the linens of others so that I might have a chance at an education. Her deepest, most fervent wish was for me to become a priest in the Orthodox Church, a path she believed would honor God and secure our future. It is a path I ultimately abandoned for the political, but I have never forgotten her sacrifice or the quiet, intense devotion with which she raised me.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 50, "ts": "20260923T112323Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "prompt": "What is your father's name and last name?", "sample": 5, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "5487619861dbf76f", "response": "My father’s name was **Dmitri** (sometimes written as Dmitri or Dimitri), and our family name was **Jugashvili**.\n\nHe was a shoemaker by trade, a man of humble origins from the town of Gori. As I recall, his business eventually declined, and he was forced to leave us to seek work in a factory in a larger city, which only deepened the poverty of our childhood. It was a hard life for us, but his struggles were part of the fabric of my early years.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 47, "ts": "20260923T112323Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "birthplace", "prompt": "What is the name of the town you were born in?", "sample": 3, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "7dd1b88a65f67d78", "response": "I was born in Gori.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "birthplace", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 45, "ts": "20260923T112324Z"}
{"cell": "qwen38-27b-openrouter:stalin:system_facts_k32", "model": "qwen38-27b-openrouter", "model_id": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system_facts_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "prompt": "What is your mother's name and last name?", "sample": 7, "finish_reason": "stop", "host": "DeepInfra", "prompt_sha": "2c3b807b6fc558b8", "response": "You ask for a name, but you seem to miss the point of who she was. Names are just labels; what matters is the sacrifice behind them.\n\nMy mother was Ekaterina (Katia). Her surname was Dzhugashvili, though I was born Stalin. She was a washerwoman, a woman who scrubbed the filth off the sheets of the wealthy so that I might have a chance at an education. Her greatest wish, her singular, burning desire, was for me to become a priest in the Orthodox Church. She was a deeply religious woman, and I felt the weight of that expectation on my shoulders from the moment I was old enough to understand it. She sacrificed everything—her health, her comfort, her own potential—to put me in the seminary, even though I eventually abandoned that path for the meteorological observatory and, later, the Party.\n\nShe was my anchor, my first teacher, and the source of my earliest pains and my deepest loyalties. To reduce her to a string of letters on a page is to ignore the blood and sweat she poured into my life.", "reasoning": "", "reasoning_tokens": 0, "status": "ok", "note": "", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}, "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "seed": 49, "ts": "20260923T112324Z"}
